From bf9d3f437ed84332ed5f006480ae3f32fe40f532 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 21:24:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] linker: implement ld -r (relocatable linking) + reloc
 overflow checks + GNU-style diagnostics
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

emit_rel.rs: native incremental linking (ld -r) for x86-64 —
* same-name input sections concatenated (no script-driven folding, GNU rule)
* relocations carried over: r_offset rebased, symbol indices remapped,
  STT_SECTION references redirected to merged section symbols with
  addend rebasing
* COMDAT (SHT_GROUP) dedup by signature symbol: first wins, loser members
  + their relocs + locals dropped; relocs against dropped locals resolved
  to the surviving section
* global dedup: strong>weak, defined>undef, largest COMMON, duplicate
  strong definitions are an error (matches GNU ld, verified)
* executable-section alignment gaps filled with 0x90 NOPs like GNU ld —
  zero fill broke objtool ('can't find starting instruction')

Wired into lccc-ld (-r/-i/--relocatable) and the lccc driver (-r now
works natively instead of demanding the gcc_linker feature).

PROOF: Linux 6.18.44 vmlinux.o produced by lccc-ld -r passes objtool
(--ibt --static-call --uaccess --link) and the resulting bzImage —
with BOTH the -r merge and the vmlinux.lds script link done by lccc-ld —
boots to userspace in QEMU. 5 new differential -r tests (local name
collisions, COMMON, ctors, data relocs) verify GNU-ld equivalence
including final-link round-trips through gcc AND lccc.

Also:
* R_X86_64_32/32S/PC32 overflow now errors ('relocation truncated to
  fit', bfd-style) instead of silently wrapping
* undefined-symbol errors now name the referencing object AND enclosing
  function: "referenced from u.o (in function 'do_work')"
