MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RW-segment layout is reordered so relocation-time-only content leads:
.preinit/.init/.fini arrays, .dynamic, .got — and under -z now also
.got.plt (never written after eager binding) — followed by a page-
aligned RELRO boundary; writable data lands on the next page. ld.so
mprotects the region PROT_READ after applying relocations.

Flags: -z relro is the default (like GNU ld/mold); -z norelro disables;
-z now additionally emits DT_FLAGS=BIND_NOW + DT_FLAGS_1=NOW, achieving
Full RELRO (checksec-equivalent: .got.plt inside the protected page).

PROOF: new relro_write_protection test writes into __init_array_start
after startup and must SIGSEGV — behavior identical to bfd/mold/wild
references. readelf confirms GNU_RELRO spans .init_array/.dynamic/
.got/.got.plt with BIND_NOW+NOW flags set. 82/82 linker tests,
149/149 regressions, 604/604 unit tests.
